## Request

Build the smallest complete correction to the App Server fleet screen. Reuse the existing local
execution telemetry and routing event stores, send only bounded aggregates, and present readiness,
reliability, and sizing evidence without exposing content or implying unsupported cost or GUI
comparisons.

## Contract Decisions

- An attempt is one top-level planning, verification, or CAMP execution.
- Preference changes, backend selections, and recovery-control events are not attempts.
- Readiness is current runtime posture; use and performance are bounded historical observations.
- Planning and verification completion remains distinct from CAMP verified completion.
- The report carries bounded 24-hour, 7-day, and 30-day rollups; the screen defaults to 7 days and
  displays the selected window explicitly.
- Performance is segmented by role and uses duration, token, cache, and weighted-usage proxy
  aggregates. Unknown historical classification remains unknown.
- The hosted payload remains strict, bounded, and content-free.

## Work2 Boundary

Implement the local aggregate, schema, persistence, migration, and page changes; run focused
aggregation/privacy/ingest/rendering tests and quick changed-path validation; commit the scoped
candidate; deploy to the combined live `ts.rookaro.com` work target; check public health and the
authenticated App Server page; register the candidate and open owning chain in the release cohort;
checkpoint and rebuild-prove Hybrid state; and run strict Doctor.

Do not push, tag, publish a release, add retained trend analytics, manufacture GUI baselines, claim
billing cost, or close the Campaign, PRM, or Map before later Work5 evidence.

## App Server Preparation Contract

Stable intent: implement the bounded Work2 vertical slice described above. Exact paths, context,
verification commands, and budgets are resolved at dispatch time if the dedicated App Server CAMP
route is selected; ordinary GUI execution remains valid.
